# sys_exit_group.tkr — the §16 FIRST-PROOF fixture. `main.tks` calls
# `teko::sys::syscall1(sys::SYS_EXIT_GROUP, 42)`, the raw x86_64 Linux `exit_group(42)`
# syscall. `exit_group` terminates ALL threads of the process immediately with the given status —
# it never returns, so the trailing `exit(0)` in `main.tks` is dead code kept only so the tree
# stays well-typed. The harness therefore observes exit code 42, proving the §16 `syscall1`
# codegen intrinsic (checker signature + preamble helper + dispatch) issued the real instruction
# and the kernel honoured it.

Feature: sys_exit_group — the §16 raw-syscall intrinsic issues x86_64 Linux exit_group(42)

  Scenario: raw_exit_group_sets_exit_code — the process exits 42 via the syscall instruction
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 42
